# Pairs with TenantRuleConfinement. This is the compiler as it stood when
# #6210 was found: CompiledTenantPartition.Build re-validates an arriving
# tenant rule, but an operator rule is compiled as found, so one naming another
# tenant's group on this tenant's tree, arriving by replication or restore,
# takes effect with an operator-final verdict.
MODULE: CompileSkipsOperatorGroupSubject
TARGET: TenantRuleConfinement
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the snapshot compiler re-validates only tenant-tier rules, not an operator rule's tenant group subject

--- FIND
CompileAdmits(r) == (r.layer = "tenant" => TenantRuleShapeOk(r)) /\ GroupSubjectOk(r)
--- REPLACE
CompileAdmits(r) == r.layer = "tenant" => TenantRuleShapeOk(r)
--- END
